h1. Weekly fleet check: last 7 days vs the previous 8 weeks

One combined HTML report across every DB in {{fleet.conf}}. Current window = the last 7 days; baseline = the same 7-day window in each of the 8 preceding weeks (9 windows total). Read-only: SELECT on the DBA_HIST views only, safe on standbys.

h2. Prerequisites (once)

* {{fleet.conf}} in the repo root, one {{alias|connect[|detail]}} per line (already done).
* {{sqlplus}} on PATH; run from the repo root (the wrapper cd's there itself).
* {{timeout}} or {{gtimeout}} on PATH, otherwise per-DB timeouts are not enforced (macOS: {{brew install coreutils}}).
* *AWR retention >= 63 days on every DB* (default is 8). Check and fix:
{code:sql}
SELECT retention FROM dba_hist_wr_control;
EXEC DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY.MODIFY_SNAPSHOT_SETTINGS(retention => 70*24*60);
{code}
Without it, baseline windows are missing and findings degrade to {{insufficient history}} (z-scores need at least 3 valid prior windows).

h2. Run (Monday morning)

Anchor the window end at Monday 00:00 of the current week so the current window is exactly last Mon 00:00 to Sun 24:00, and every baseline window is the same Mon-Sun in the prior 8 weeks:

{code:bash}
./run_awr_fleet.sh fleet.conf '2026-08-31 00:00' 168 8
{code}

Positional args, left to right: {{fleet.conf}}, {{target_end}}, {{win_hours}}, {{weeks_back}}, {{top_n}} (default 10), {{step}} (default 1), {{step_unit}} (default w). {{168 8}} = 7-day window, 8 prior weeks, weekly cadence; the last three defaults are what you want.

Rolling alternative (7 days ending at the last full hour, no fixed anchor):

{code:bash}
./run_awr_fleet.sh fleet.conf AUTO 168 8
{code}

Cron (Monday 06:00; {{date +%F}} on a Monday is that Monday):

{code}
0 6 * * 1  cd /path/to/awr_timeline_comparison && FLEET_QUIET=1 ./run_awr_fleet.sh fleet.conf "$(date +\%F) 00:00" 168 8 >> logs/fleet.log 2>&1
{code}

h2. Useful env knobs (prefix to the command)

|| Var || Default || Use ||
| {{FLEET_PAR}} | 4 | concurrent sqlplus runs; raise for big fleets |
| {{FLEET_TIMEOUT}} | 900 | per-DB seconds for the fleet extract. 7-day windows scan more history, use 1800 on busy DBs |
| {{FLEET_DETAIL}} | (per conf line) | {{all}} = full single-DB report for every DB, {{none}} = skip all |
| {{FLEET_DETAIL_TIMEOUT}} | 3600 | per-DB seconds for the detailed report, 0 = unlimited |
| {{MARKERS}} | (empty) | inline timeline markers, vertical lines on every ASH timeline; format below |
| {{MARKER_FILE}} | (empty) | file of WHEN-pipe-LABEL lines, wins over MARKERS |
| {{FLEET_KEEP_WORK}} | 0 | 1 keeps the per-DB logs dir even on success |
| {{FLEET_QUIET}} | 0 | 1 silences progress narration (cron) |

Marker format, {{WHEN|LABEL}} pairs joined by {{;;}}:
{code:bash}
MARKERS='2026-08-28 14:00|Patch 19.28;;2026-08-30 02:00|Storage move' ./run_awr_fleet.sh fleet.conf '2026-08-31 00:00' 168 8
{code}

h2. Output

* {{reports/awr\_fleet\_<ts>\_run<id>/index.html}} is the console. {{detail\_<alias>.html}} beside it for every {{|detail}} DB. The folder is self-contained and offline (no CDN); archive or copy it anywhere, links stay valid.
* stdout ends with a per-DB summary line and {{Report: <path>}}.
* Exit 0 = at least one DB OK, 3 = every DB failed, 2 = bad args/conf (nothing ran).

h2. Reading it (5 minutes)

# *Masthead*: N databases / crit / warn / quiet / unreachable. Check the *Compared windows* strip: dashed chips = skipped windows (hover for the reason: no snapshot, restart inside window, DBID change). Many skipped = retention or a restart; with a 7-day window *any* restart in that week invalidates it for that DB.
# *Rows* are error rows first, then by score = {{10*crit + 3*warn + min(25, Top-SQL points)}}. A row shows the worst finding, AAS, a DB-time sparkline across the 9 windows, and an ASH ribbon.
# *Click a row*: ASH timeline by wait class and by event over the full 9-week span, metric mini-cards (current vs baseline, z-score), findings, Top SQL that moved, and a ready-made drill command for the full single-DB report.
# *Error rows* carry the masked connect string, the ORA-/TNS- code, and the last 15 log lines. Fix creds/TNS and rerun; the good rows do not need rerunning.
# Numbers are 7-day averages: daily peaks are smoothed, Top SQL ranks by 7-day cumulative cost. Drill into the detailed report (or run a 1-hour window with {{step_unit d}}) when a finding needs a time-of-day view.

h2. When it goes wrong

* All rows failed (exit 3): workdir kept at {{reports/fleet\_work\_<id>/}}, read {{<alias>.log}}. Typical: ORA-12514 (service), ORA-01017 (creds), ORA-00942 (missing SELECT_CATALOG_ROLE / Diagnostic Pack), rc=124 (timeout, raise FLEET_TIMEOUT).
* Reassemble without touching any DB:
{code:bash}
./run_awr_fleet.sh --assemble reports/fleet_work_<id>
{code}
* Metric cards all n/a or skip: no valid windows. Verify snapshots exist at the window edges ({{dba_hist_snapshot}}); the wrapper snaps {{target_end}} back to the last snapshot when none is within 15 min, and the drill panel says so.
* {{./run_awr_fleet.sh --help}} prints the full argument and env reference.
